layout: false
liquid: true
markdown: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The full documentation for language models, in starlight-llms-txt 0.11's format (llms-full.txt.ts and
  generator.ts): a <SYSTEM> line, then for each root-locale page that is not a draft "# <hero title or title>",
  "> <hero tagline or description>" and the page's Markdown, separated by blank lines. As in the plugin, the
  `exclude` option does not apply to this file (only to llms-small.txt).

  Assumes a collect step over the Markdown twins (Douze plan 3.12):
    llms-docs: { needs: twins, uses: collect, match: "**/*.md", with: { name: docs, content: true } }
  so `docs.all` lists the twins and `item.content` is a page's Markdown after Liquid (shortcodes resolved to
  HTML, %ASPIRE_VERSION% replaced, no front matter). The plugin converts the rendered HTML back to Markdown
  instead (tabs as lists, code blocks from Expressive Code, twoslash popups removed); the twins are the
  Markdown source with the components' HTML inline, which carries the same text. Twoslash popups do not exist
  in the twins (the code worker runs on the HTML), so the plugin's customSelectors are not needed.
  Order: by url (ordinal; the plugin promotes `index*` to the top, which the root url already is, then sorts the
  ids with an English collation).

  Filters: sort_by (planned, Douze plan 3.12), locale_of (planned, 3.6, used when the item has no `locale`); default, strip, replace, append (Liquid).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture nl %}
{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign separator = nl | append: nl -%}
{%- assign pages = docs.all | sort_by: "data.url" -%}
<SYSTEM>This is the full developer documentation for {{ site.llms.project_name | default: site.title }}</SYSTEM>
{%- for item in pages -%}
  {%- assign data = item.data -%}
  {%- if data.draft -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign item_locale = item.data.locale -%}
  {%- unless item_locale -%}{%- assign item_locale = item.data.url | locale_of -%}{%- endunless -%}
  {%- if item_locale != "default" -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {{ separator }}# {{ data.hero.title | default: data.title }}
  {%- assign summary = data.hero.tagline | default: data.description -%}
  {%- if summary -%}{{ separator }}> {{ summary }}{%- endif -%}
  {{ separator }}{{ item.content | strip }}
{%- endfor -%}
